Okay, so Ned had to wash a bunch of shirts before school. Let me try to figure out how many shirts he didn't wash. The problem says he had to wash 9 short sleeve shirts and 21 long sleeve shirts. First, I need to find out the total number of shirts he needed to wash. 

So, adding the short sleeve and long sleeve shirts together: 9 plus 21. Let me calculate that. 9 + 21 is 30. So, he had 30 shirts in total to wash.

Then the problem says that before school started, he had only washed 29 of them. Wait, so he washed 29 shirts by the time school started? So, the question is asking how many he did not wash. That would be the total number of shirts minus the ones he washed. 

So, total shirts are 30, and he washed 29. Therefore, 30 minus 29 equals 1. So, he didn't wash 1 shirt. 

Let me check again to make sure I didn't make a mistake. The numbers: 9 short sleeve and 21 long sleeve. 9 + 21 is indeed 30. He washed 29, so 30 - 29 is 1. Yeah, that seems right. So the answer is 1. 

