Now, the coach is dividing them into groups of 6 players each. To find out how many groups there are, I need to divide the total number of players by the number of players per group. So that would be 54 divided by 6. Let me do that division. 54 ÷ 6. Hmm, 6 times 9 is 54, right? So 6 multiplied by 9 equals 54. Therefore, 54 divided by 6 is 9.

